Subject: Stop writing uninitialised list slack into GC records

gc_store_retired() reserves a GC record sized for `chunk_hi` page numbers --
`left_before | 3`, so up to three more than the list holds -- and then copies
data.iov_len bytes from the retired-pages list into it. Only the first `chunk`
entries are the record; the count at its head says so, and every reader goes
by the count. The bytes after them are whatever lies past the end of the list:
the uninitialised slack of its malloc() block from pnl_alloc(), which the
commit then writes to disk.

CRAN's valgrind run of 0.1.1 reported it as

    Syscall param pwritev(vector[1]) points to uninitialised byte(s)
    Syscall param pwrite64(buf) points to uninitialised byte(s)
      Uninitialised value was created by a heap allocation
        at malloc / by pnl_alloc / by txn_basal_create

two contexts, from the commit path. The package's CI had suppressed these as
"page padding" (tools/valgrind.supp); --track-origins=yes, which CRAN uses,
shows the origin is the list, not the page: page_shadow_alloc() zeroes every
page it hands out.

This copies gc_chunk_bytes(chunk) bytes and zeroes the rest of the
reservation. The record's contents up to its count are unchanged, so is its
size, and the zeroed tail is never read. It also stops the copy reading up to
three entries past the end of the list.

--- a/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c
+++ b/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c
@@ -23947,7 +23947,12 @@
          *    and should be placed with the smaller txnid. */
         const pgno_t save = *begin;
         *begin = (pgno_t)chunk;
-        memcpy(data.iov_base, begin, data.iov_len);
+        /* R package patch: copy the `chunk` entries the record holds and zero
+         * the rest of the reservation, rather than copying data.iov_len bytes
+         * -- sized for chunk_hi -- which reads past the end of the list into
+         * uninitialised slack and writes it to disk. See tools/patches. */
+        memcpy(data.iov_base, begin, gc_chunk_bytes(chunk));
+        memset(ptr_disp(data.iov_base, gc_chunk_bytes(chunk)), 0, data.iov_len - gc_chunk_bytes(chunk));
         *begin = save;
         TRACE("%s: put-retired/bigfoot @ %" PRIaTXN " (slice #%u) #%zu [%zu..%zu] of %zu", dbg_prefix(ctx),
               ctx->bigfoot, (unsigned)(ctx->bigfoot - txn->txnid), chunk, at, at + chunk, retired_before);
